  "subtitle": "The keytar whose neck is a ribbon controller you play by touch",
  "blurb": "One of the first commercial keytars (1980), the Liberation is a synthesizer you wear on a strap like a guitar. Its most distinctive control is a long ribbon controller running the length of the neck: the player's finger position and pressure along it glides and bends pitch — a continuous, expressive surface in place of keys or knobs.",
